                        "answer": 0
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "phase": "grammar",
                  "type": "grammar_rule",
                  "content": {
                    "title": "Linkers of contrast",
                    "explanation": "Para contraponer ideas:\n• although / even though + sujeto + verbo: Although I like the colours, it feels too simple. (Even though es más enfático.)\n• despite / in spite of + nombre o -ing: In spite of being simple, it's faster. Despite that, …\n• however / nevertheless empiezan una frase nueva y van seguidos de coma: However, our research shows… (Nevertheless es más formal.)\n• whereas contrasta dos hechos: Your site takes ten seconds, whereas this one takes two.\n\nPara opinar en una reunión: If I may…, I agree with…, I'm not sure about…, We don't see eye to eye, Don't sit on the fence.",
                    "table": {
                      "headers": [
                        "Conector",
                        "Va seguido de",
                        "Ejemplo"
                      ],
                      "rows": [
                        [
                          "although / even though",
                          "sujeto + verbo",
                          "Although I like the colours, it feels too simple."
                        ],
                        [
                          "despite / in spite of",
                          "nombre o -ing",
                          "In spite of being simple, it's faster."
                        ],
                        [
                          "however",
                          "nueva frase + coma",
                          "However, our research shows…"
                        ],
                        [
                          "nevertheless",
                          "nueva frase (más formal)",
                          "Nevertheless, I need two versions."
                        ],
                        [
                          "whereas",
                          "contraste entre dos hechos",
                          "Yours takes ten seconds, whereas ours takes two."
                        ]
                      ]
                    },
                    "examples": [
                      "Although I like the colours, the homepage feels too simple.",
                      "Despite that, I think luxury needs more photos.",
                      "I agree with Lucía, even though you're paying the bill.",
                      "Nevertheless, I need to see two versions."
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "phase": "grammar",
                  "type": "grammar_rule",
                  "content": {
                    "title": "Formal discourse markers: furthermore, moreover, consequently",
                    "explanation": "En reuniones, presentaciones y textos formales organizamos las ideas con marcadores:\n\n• Para empezar y ordenar: To begin with, Firstly, Secondly, Finally.\n• Para añadir: Furthermore, Moreover, In addition (además), Additionally.\n• Para la consecuencia: Consequently, As a result, Therefore (por consiguiente).\n• Para introducir un tema: Regarding / As regards the budget (en cuanto al presupuesto).\n• Para contrastar dos puntos de vista: On the one hand… On the other hand…\n• Para cerrar: In conclusion, To sum up (en resumen).\n\nVan al principio de la frase, seguidos de coma. En una conversación informal suenan demasiado formales: con amigos se dice also, so o anyway.",
                    "table": {
                      "headers": [
                        "Función",
                        "Marcadores",
                        "Ejemplo"
                      ],
                      "rows": [
                        [
                          "Añadir",
                          "furthermore, moreover, in addition",
                          "Moreover, it loads in two seconds."
                        ],
                        [
                          "Consecuencia",
                          "consequently, as a result",
                          "Consequently, guests book more quickly."
                        ],
                        [
                          "Tema",
                          "regarding, as regards",
                          "Regarding the photos, we'll add a gallery."
                        ],
                        [
                          "Dos puntos de vista",
                          "on the one hand… on the other hand",
                          "On the one hand it's simple; on the other hand it looks cheap."
                        ],
                        [
                          "Cerrar",
                          "in conclusion, to sum up",
                          "To sum up, simple sells."
                        ]
                      ]
                    },
                    "examples": [
                      "To begin with, I'd like to show you our research.",
                      "Furthermore, the new site loads five times faster.",
                      "Guests find what they want quickly. Consequently, they book more rooms.",
                      "In conclusion, we recommend the simple version."
                    ]
                  }
                },
